_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.46453997,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"ProKidney Corp., a clinical-stage biotechnology company, engages in the development of cell therapies for the treatment of chronic kidney diseases in the United States. The company develops rilparencel, a cell therapy with autologous selected renal cells, which is in Phase III clinical trial for the treatment of advanced chronic kidney disease and type 2 diabetes. It is also involved in the development of cryopreserved versions of rilparencel, including REGEN-006 and REGEN-008 which are both in Phase III clinical trials; REGEN-002, REGEN-003, and REGEN-007 which are in Phase II clinical trials; and REGEN-004 which is Phase I clinical trial. The company was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in Winston-Salem, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Bruce  Culleton M.D. | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 231 people. Revenue per employee of $4K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $110K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 306\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["ProKidney Corp. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $417M market cap on $893,000 of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1075% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $135M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +15.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -41251.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 5.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 2837% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 46% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +15.2% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 18477% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 141% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ProKidney (NASDAQ:PROK) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Expectations By $0.04 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/prokidney-nasdaqprok-posts-quarterly-earnings-results-misses-expectations-by-0-04-eps.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794532257.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ProKidney Corp. (PROK) Reports Q3 Loss, Misses Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029071/prokidney-corp-prok-reports-q3-loss-misses-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3029071","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794521105.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Analysts\u2019 Price Target Changes for October 28th (ABG, AWI, BRSP, CLS, CNC, COMP, FCX, LFTO, PROK, ST)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/28/analysts-price-target-changes-for-october-28th-abg-awi-brsp-cls-cnc-comp-fcx-lfto-prok-st.html","date":"2026-10-28","timestamp":1793231068.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.25,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Contrasting CytomX Therapeutics (NASDAQ:CTMX) & ProKidney (NASDAQ:PROK)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/20/contrasting-cytomx-therapeutics-nasdaq